{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Human-Computer Interaction.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Human-Computer Interaction.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"human computer interaction human computer interaction","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Human-Computer Interaction.md","fileName":"Human-Computer Interaction.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Human-Computer Interaction","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 13:11\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Human-Computer Interaction Foundations]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Human-Computer Interaction Foundations","User Interface","Perception","Cognition","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Human-Computer Interaction.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Human-Computer Interaction.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"human computer interaction human computer interaction","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Human-Computer Interaction.md","fileName":"Human-Computer Interaction.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Human-Computer Interaction","heading":"Human-Computer Interaction","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Human-computer interaction studies the relationship and communication between people and interactive technology. People communicate actions, goals, and queries to a system, while the system communicates its state and responses through a [[User Interface]].\n\nThe field places human needs first and draws on knowledge of [[Perception]], [[Cognition]], and physical action. It includes both understanding existing interactions and designing new ones, from devices and gestures to computer-mediated collaboration. Effectiveness depends on the purpose: task performance may dominate a work system, while engagement or emotional impact may matter more in a game or artwork.\n\nHCI design the